m;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How bad is flood risk in Pawleys Island?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">High. Public data flags around 89 percent of properties as facing severe flood risk over 30 years, so flood insurance and elevation certificates are essential considerations for any purchase.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Which schools serve Pawleys Island?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Public schools fall within the Georgetown County School District, generally the Waccamaw schools for the Litchfield and Pawleys area. Chapter3 will confirm the exact assignment on the district boundary map.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What is Pawleys Island like?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Historic and low-key, with higher price points and more of a second-home and long-term character than mass tourism.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Who buys in Pawleys Island?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Buyers drawn to a quieter, established feel, often for second homes or longer-term ownership.</p></div></div></section>
