+</style><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Pawleys Island is a barrier island less than 4 miles long and mostly one house wide, with salt marsh between it and the mainland. Two short causeways, the North Causeway and the South Causeway, cross the marsh.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Town of Pawleys Island is the island itself, a town of its own since 1985. Everything on the mainland with a Pawleys Island address is unincorporated Georgetown County. The island and most of the mainland around it share ZIP code 29585, so a Pawleys Island address does not mean a house on the island.</p><figure class="c3-pi-fig"><div class="c3-pi-frame"><svg class="c3-pi-map" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1400 1603" role="img" aria-labelledby="c3-pi-map-t"><title id="c3-pi-map-t">Aerial map of Pawleys Island, South Carolina, and the mainland around it. The island is a thin strip along the ocean with salt marsh behind it; its town limits are outlined. Two causeways cross the marsh to the mainland. US 17 runs inland, parallel to the coast. Number 1 is the island, 2 is Litchfield to the north, 3 is the mainland behind the island, and 4 is west of US 17.</title><image href="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-area-aerial-1000.webp" x="0" y="0" width="1400" height="1603" preserveAspectRatio="none"/><path d="M538.3 1492.4L538.9 1482.1L547 1462.9L552.4 1452.1L566.8 1435.5L573.2 1421.9L578.8 1407.4L589 1386.4L596.2 1366.7L605.3 1345.7L613.3 1329.7L617.2 1319.8L619.2 1312.3L621.9 1298.1L623.1 1285.7L622 1275.4L618.3 1261.3L605.2 1246.5L603.6 1243.3L602.4 1240.2L601.8 1235.1L603.5 1229.8L607.7 1224.3L612.1 1220L624.4 1211.1L636.7 1205.3L681.6 1188L687.8 1183.5L691.2 1178.4L692.8 1173L693.3 1165.7L691.2 1158.6L688.9 1156L687 1151.8L686.5 1146.6L