57.8 484.8)"><circle r="46" fill="#8a5a9e" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="8"/><text class="pn" y="23" text-anchor="middle">4</text></g></svg></div><figcaption>The dashed line is the town limits: the island and the marsh behind it. Everything outside it is unincorporated Georgetown County, and much of it still has a Pawleys Island address. Aerial: USDA NAIP via The National Map (USGS), public domain. Lines: Georgetown County GIS. Labels: Chapter3 Realty.</figcaption><ol class="c3-pi-key" aria-label="The four parts of Pawleys Island"><li><span class="c3-pi-num z1" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span><a href="#the-island">Pawleys Island, the town</a>: the beach in front, the creek behind, about 480 houses</span></li><li><span class="c3-pi-num z2" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span><a href="#litchfield">Litchfield, ocean side of US 17</a>: north of the island, the most sales near the beach</span></li><li><span class="c3-pi-num z3" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span><a href="#behind-the-island">The mainland behind the island</a>: between US 17 and the marsh</span></li><li><span class="c3-pi-num z4" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span><a href="#west-of-17">West of US 17</a>: most of the homes, the lowest prices</span></li></ol></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The difference matters to a buyer. The island has its own building rules, its own beach rules and its own police department, and a house on it costs about four times what a mainland house costs. From the island, Broadway at the Beach in Myrtle Beach is about 40 minutes by car without traffic, and Myrtle Beach International Airport about 40 minutes.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-at-the-north-causeway-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-at-the-north-causeway-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-at-the-north-causeway-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of Pawleys Island, labelled: the North Causeway crossing the salt marsh from the mainland to the island, a narrow strip of houses, and the Atlantic Ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Pawleys Island at the North Causeway from above: the salt marsh, the causeway, and the rows of houses between the marsh and the beach.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Home prices">How much do homes cost on Pawleys Island and the mainland?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An island house sold for about $2.45 million at the middle over the last three years, and half sold for between about $1.9 million and $2.65 million. On the mainland a house sold for about $580,000 west of US 17 and about $675,000 between US 17 and the marsh, in the past year.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:49.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Houses with a Pawleys Island address, by part</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Houses</th><th scope="col" class="n">Middle sale, past year</th><th scope="col" class="n">Houses sold, past year</th><th scope="col">In a high-risk flood zone</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#the-island" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Pawleys Island, the town</a></th><td data-label="Houses">About 480</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle sale, past year">$2,450,000</td><td class="n" data-label="Houses sold, past year">10</td><td data-label="In a high-risk flood zone">All but 1</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#litchfield" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Litchfield, ocean side of US 17</a></th><td data-label="Houses">About 1,200</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle sale, past year">$1,250,000</td><td class="n" data-label="Houses sold, past year">50</td><td data-label="In a high-risk flood zone">97 in 100</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#behind-the-island" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Mainland behind the island</a></th><td data-label="Houses">About 1,200</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle sale, past year">$675,000</td><td class="n" data-label="Houses sold, past year">53</td><td data-label="In a high-risk flood zone">About 1 in 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#west-of-17" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">West of US 17</a></th><td data-label="Houses">About 4,800</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle sale, past year">$580,000</td><td class="n" data-label="Houses sold, past year">220</td><td data-label="In a high-risk flood zone">About 1 in 20</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Middle sale: half of the houses sold for more, half for less. These are houses only, from every deed Georgetown County recorded. The numbers in the table match the map above.</p><h3 id="the-island" data-toc="the island" class="c3-pi-h3"><span class="c3-pi-num z1" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span>Pawleys Island, the town: the beach in front, the creek behind</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 480 houses stand on the island, and about 220 of them face the ocean. The rest look onto the marsh and the creek or stand between the two roads. Oceanfront houses sold for about $2.6 million at the middle over three years, and houses on the creek side for about $2 million.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No other part has houses this old, or this few sales. It is also the most exposed to the water; the flood and setback sections below cover what that means.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Pawleys%20Island">Get the houses for sale on Pawleys Island<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="litchfield" data-toc="Litchfield" class="c3-pi-h3"><span class="c3-pi-num z2" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span>Litchfield, ocean side of US 17: the most sales near the beach</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North of the island, Litchfield's ocean side of US 17 has about 1,200 houses. More of them sell: 50 in the past year, at about $1.25 million at the middle. Its 155 oceanfront houses sold for about $3.6 million at the middle over three years, more than oceanfront houses on Pawleys Island.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Like the island, 97 in 100 of its houses are in a high-risk flood zone.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Litchfield">Get the homes for sale in Litchfield<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="behind-the-island" data-toc="behind the island" class="c3-pi-h3"><span class="c3-pi-num z3" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span>The mainland behind the island: between US 17 and the marsh</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South of Litchfield, the mainland between US 17 and the marsh has about 1,200 houses, including Pawleys Plantation. A house here sold for about $675,000 at the middle in the past year, from 53 sales. About a third of the houses are in a high-risk flood zone.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We get the homeowners association's papers for any mainland community before you offer. The prices of the named gated communities are on our <a href="/buyers/gated-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">gated communities page</a>.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Pawleys%20Island">Get the homes for sale behind Pawleys Island<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="west-of-17" data-toc="west of US 17" class="c3-pi-h3"><span class="c3-pi-num z4" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span>West of US 17: most of the homes, the lowest prices</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">West of US 17 are most of the homes with a Pawleys Island address: about 4,800 houses. A house here sold for about $580,000 at the middle in the past year, from 220 sales, and a condo for about $320,000. Only about 1 in 20 houses is in a high-risk flood zone.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Pawleys%20Island">Get the homes for sale west of US 17 in Pawleys Island<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">For sale now</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At our last count there were 279 listings with a Pawleys Island address. Only 4 were on the island, and 2 of those were houses, asking about $3 million and $3.45 million. Across the whole address, the middle asking price was about $815,000 for a house and about $315,000 for a condo or townhouse.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="second-home-pawleys-island" data-name="Pawleys Island" data-head="For sale on and near the island"></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="how-often"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="How often one sells">How often does a house on Pawleys Island come up for sale?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Rarely. In the past five years at least 44 of the island's 480 houses were bought at a market price, about 1 in 11. On Litchfield's ocean side and west of US 17, houses were bought at a market price about twice as often.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Houses bought at a market price in the past five years"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Houses bought at a market price in the past five years</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Part</span><span role="columnheader">Share of houses</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pawleys Island, the town</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.368" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 1 in 11</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Litchfield, ocean side of US 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.74" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 1 in 5</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">West of US 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.784" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 1 in 5</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>At least: the county keeps only the last deed on each house, so a house sold and later deeded to a trust counts as not sold. That is true in every part. Georgetown County records; a market sale is a deed of $10,000 or more.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Island houses stay in families. On about 6 in 10 of them, the last recorded transfer was not a sale: the deed shows under $1,000, the kind of deed used to pass a house to heirs or a trust, or to move it into a company. West of US 17 it is 1 in 3.</p><ul class="c3-pi-stats" aria-label="How island houses change hands"><li><b>About 6 in 10</b><span>island houses last passed by a deed under $1,000</span></li><li><b>About 1 in 10</b><span>island houses unsold since before 2000</span></li><li><b>12 new, 7 gone</b><span>buildings on the island between the 2017 and 2024 county surveys</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town says many houses in its historic district belong to the third, fourth or fifth generation of one family, and that in 2012 one house, Liberty Lodge, marked 100 years in a single family.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">What it means for you: the house you want may come up once in years, and the island is built out, so few new ones are added. Tell us what you want, and we call you when a house like it comes up.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Pawleys%20Island">Ask us to watch for a house on Pawleys Island<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="flooding"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flooding">Does Pawleys Island flood, and what does flood insurance cost?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town works to lower what island owners pay for flood insurance. It takes part in FEMA's Community Rating System at Class 5, which takes 25 percent off flood insurance premiums on the island. FEMA's base flood elevation for island houses is 12 to 16 feet, and the town requires a new house to sit 3 feet higher than that.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every island house but one is in one of FEMA's high-risk flood zones: about half in the VE zone, where waves are expected, and half in AE. A lender making a mortgage on any of them will require flood insurance. The south end is the most exposed: 93 in 100 houses south of the South Causeway are in the VE zone, against fewer than 1 in 10 north of the North Causeway.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What flood insurance costs</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A federal flood policy on an island house that is not its owner's main home cost about $4,770 a year at the middle. On a house that is the owner's main home it was about $1,680, and on a mainland house in the same ZIP code about $1,050.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What a federal flood policy on a house cost a year, at the middle"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What a federal flood policy on a house cost a year, at the middle</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">House</span><span role="columnheader">A year</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Island house, not the owner's main home</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$4,770</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Island house, the owner's main home</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.353" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,680</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Mainland house, same ZIP code</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.22" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,050</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>FEMA's flood insurance policies on single-family houses that began June 2025 to May 2026, ZIP 29585. Island: the Town of Pawleys Island's policies. Mainland: the Georgetown County policies in the same ZIP code. The cost includes FEMA's fees.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most island policies carry $250,000 of building coverage, the federal program's limit for a home. A house worth $2.45 million needs private flood coverage for the rest. We get the flood zone, the elevation certificate and the current policy for any house before you offer. Our page on <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance</a> explains wind and flood coverage.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">King tides</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town's own drainage problem is roadside flooding at the highest tides of the year, the king tides. It adopted a sea level rise plan and a master drainage plan for the whole island, and the plan's final draft went to the town council in December 2025.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="rebuild"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Rebuilding on the ocean">Can you rebuild an oceanfront house on Pawleys Island?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, within limits that matter most at the south end. The state draws two lines along the beach: a baseline at the crest of the front dune, and a setback line 20 feet landward of it. On about 100 of the island's roughly 220 oceanfront houses, part of the house stands on the ocean side of the setback line: 78 of 138 at the south end. On Litchfield's ocean side it is 86 of 155.</p><figure class="c3-pi-fig narrow"><div class="c3-pi-frame"><svg class="c3-pi-inset" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="400 100 1200 1650" role="img" aria-labelledby="c3-pi-inset-t"><title id="c3-pi-inset-t">Aerial map of the south end of Pawleys Island: one row of oceanfront houses between the creek and the beach. The state's baseline at the dune crest and its setback line 20 feet landward of it run through the row of houses. Most of the houses in this stretch are shaded, meaning part of the house is on the ocean side of the setback line.</title><image href="/images/20