+What is a Section 1316 designation, and how does it impact 
+food insurance availability? 
+If a building is constructed in a way that violates state or local ordinances 
+related to foodplain management, it is given a Section 1316 designation. 
+The designation occurs as a last resort to a building determined not in 
+compliance with local ordinances related to foodplain management, after 
+being determined substantially damaged, and not being brought into 
+compliance standards. Contents and personal property contained in these 
+buildings are ineligible for coverage. The NFIP's food insurance is not 
+available for buildings with a Section 1316 designation. A community offcial 
+may request that FEMA rescind the Section 1316 designation when the 
+structure is determined compliant with the foodplain management laws, 
+regulations, or ordinances. 
