+        + `<li><strong>Repair</strong>A house damaged by a storm, but not destroyed, can be repaired.</li>`
+        + `<li><strong>Rebuild</strong>A house a storm destroys can be rebuilt only if it is no larger past the setback line, no wider along the beach and no farther seaward than before, moved landward where possible, and never past the baseline.</li>`
+        + `<li><strong>New house</strong>A new house built partly past the setback line may have at most 5,000 square feet of heated space.</li>`
+        + `<li><strong>The town's own line</strong>The town draws its own Shore Protection Line, which is usually stricter than the state's.</li>`
+        + `</ul>` +
+      h.p(`Before you offer on an oceanfront house, we get the survey and the elevation certificate and see where both lines fall on the lot.`) +
